<!--
  Share card for the manual (#527). mdBook injects this into every page's <head>.

  What is here is what mdBook can state correctly without inventing anything.
  `{{ title }}` is the page's own chapter title, so og:title is per page rather
  than the one book title repeated 35 times.

  What is deliberately NOT here: `og:url` and `<link rel=canonical>`. Both need
  the absolute URL a reader actually lands on, and mdBook offers only
  `{{ path }}`, which is the *source* path (`concepts/the-ledger.md`). The site
  serves these extensionless and redirects `.html` to bare, so a tag built from
  `{{ path }}` would name a URL that redirects, and a canonical pointing at a
  redirect is worse than no canonical: it splits the signal instead of joining
  it. Handlebars here has no string helpers to strip the extension, so doing
  this right means rewriting the built HTML after mdBook runs. Left out on
  purpose rather than shipped wrong.
-->
<meta property="og:type" content="article" />
<meta property="og:site_name" content="VENG" />
<meta property="og:title" content="{{ title }}" />
<meta property="og:image" content="https://veng.weekndlabs.com/media/og.png" />
<meta property="og:image:width" content="2400" />
<meta property="og:image:height" content="1260" />
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
<meta name="twitter:title" content="{{ title }}" />
<meta name="twitter:image" content="https://veng.weekndlabs.com/media/og.png" />
